To ensure robust error handling and fault tolerance, we implement robust exception handling throughout the code. Any exceptions thrown during service execution are caught and handled appropriately, preventing the system from crashing under unexpected conditions. We also include a log entry for each lifecycle transition to provide debugging information.

Unit tests have been written to validate the behavior of the `ServiceManager` class under various scenarios, such as rapid state changes and data overflow conditions. These tests cover key functionality, ensuring that the system remains stable and performant in real-world usage.']

