To integrate this program into a larger application framework, you can use the `JNI_CreateJavaVM` function provided by the Java NIO API to create a new Java Virtual Machine (JVM) instance within the C program. The JVM can then be used to run a separate Java program that handles the communication with the remote address using the Java NIO API. This approach allows for efficient integration between languages and enables the use of the Java NIO API's robust network I/O capabilities.

