The add_sensor_record() function takes a pointer to the collection of sensor records (a pointer to an array of struct SensorRecord pointers), a timestamp (long), a measurement (double), and a tag (char) as input. If there is not enough space in the existing collection, it reallocates the array with twice the current size using realloc(), and updates the total memory usage variable accordingly. It then creates a new record using allocate_sensor_record() and adds it to the collection at the end.

The remove_sensor_record() function takes a pointer to the collection of sensor records and a timestamp (long) as input, and removes the record with the given timestamp from the collection if it exists. It updates the total memory usage variable accordingly.

The get_sensor_record() function takes a pointer to the collection of sensor records and a timestamp (long) as input, and returns the record with the given timestamp if it exists in the collection. If no such record is found, it returns NULL.

The get_sensor_records() function takes a pointer to the collection of sensor records and a tag (char) as input, and retrieves all records from the collection that have the given tag. It allocates an array of pointers to SensorRecord structures to store the retrieved records, and returns it. If memory allocation fails, it prints an error message and returns NULL.

