The implementation also includes a mechanism to track the total memory usage in bytes allocated for all attacks and ensure that the function can handle up to 10 million attacks efficiently without causing a segmentation fault or excessive resource consumption. The function also provides a way to deallocate all allocated memory when done, ensuring no memory leaks occur.

