To optimize memory usage and performance, we use a configurable cache size that can be adjusted by the developer. The cache is implemented as an array of data items, which allows us to quickly retrieve recently accessed items without having to traverse the entire list. When the cache becomes full, we evict old or unused items using a least-recently-used (LRU) policy. This helps reduce memory usage while maintaining good performance.

We also implement edge cases and diverse test scenarios to thoroughly validate the implementation. For example, we test with varying data sizes, load factors, and cache eviction policies to ensure robustness and reliability under different conditions.']

