To handle real-time updates, this implementation uses a helper function `read_timestamps` to read a line of input from standard input and update the session objects accordingly. The `is_valid_timestamp` function validates the input string as an integer value before converting it to a long integer value using `atol`. The `get_activity_level` function gets the activity level of a specific session object based on its index in the list.

This implementation uses dynamic memory allocation for the session list and reallocates more memory if necessary to ensure that no segmentation faults occur. Additionally, this implementation ensures efficient memory usage by using a balanced tree data structure instead of a hash map, which requires less memory but may have slower performance during high-load scenarios.

