The function is designed to be concurrently accessed from multiple threads, using synchronization mechanisms such as mutex locks and atomic operations to avoid race conditions. It optimizes data locality by accessing elements of the record array in a way that minimizes cache misses.

The function is well-documented with performance metrics and design decisions, making it easy to maintain and enhance in the future.']

