The constructor initializes the arrays and map with sufficient capacity to handle up to 10 million records without causing a segmentation fault or excessive resource consumption. The `insertRecord` method inserts a new record into the arrays if it does not already exist, while the `deleteRecord` method removes an existing record from the arrays. The `getRecordValue` method retrieves the value associated with a given key, returning 0.0 if the record does not exist.

The class also provides a method to deallocate all allocated memory when done, ensuring no memory leaks occur. Finally, it implements a fail-safe mechanism to handle unexpected data sources or processing failures, allowing the function to recover gracefully and continue operation without interruption.']

