To handle concurrent access from multiple threads, the function uses a synchronized block to ensure that only one thread can modify the internal state at a time. The `MAX_MEMORY` constant limits the total memory usage to 1 GB, while the `MAX_RECORDS` constant sets the maximum number of records to 1 billion.

