This code also includes logging for debugging and monitoring, recording each filename modification attempt and its result, allowing easy adaptation to different environments. The logging mechanism is designed to be configurable and flexible, making it easy to integrate with existing systems.

In terms of performance optimization, this code uses a multi-threaded approach to handle concurrent operations safely, avoiding race conditions or deadlocks. It also includes an edge case handling for empty filenames and those ending with a period. The function is designed to be highly efficient, balancing efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability, making strategic trade-offs in the real-world engineering scenario.']

