The function also handles memory allocation errors gracefully, ensuring the program does not crash under unexpected input conditions. It provides a mechanism to reset memory tracking to zero after freeing all allocated memory.
Finally, it has multiple features like handling sync issues with multiple threads accessing the function concurrently, ensuring thread safety and consistent state across operations and optimizing memory usage and allocation strategies to minimize fragmentation and ensure efficient handling of large datasets.']

